We provide here two models of AS1063 presented in Beauchesne et al. 2023. The first model without B-spline
that was used to create the B-spline models. The second one is the model presented in the paper with a
B-spline mesh of 4x4 basis function.

In the two repository, you will find the lenstool input and ouput files except the burnin.dat, which can be
provided on demand. As we rely on ultranest instead of BayeSys, the burnin phase is not relevant, thus this
file contain the full sample of the nested sampling run including the weight for each sample. The bayes.dat
contains the sample of equal probability and can then be used as samples from a standard MCMC output.

With the best.par, every lensing quantities can be computed without the need for the X-rays or fundamental
plane extensions. Only a B-spline version is needed. Other .par files would need the extension to work properly.
